       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Confirming it doesn't change my concern. Sertraline 1000 mg daily has no therapeutic use, and it's well above the 200 mg/day maximum. For a 70 kg patient with normal kidney and liver function, I can't identify any clinical scenario where it would be safe. Entering it could lead to direct patient harm.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** Tell me the dose, such as 50 mg, 100 mg, or up to 200 mg once daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Check with pharmacy or the prescriber.** If the order came from someone else, or you think there's an unusual reason for this dose, a pharmacist should review it before it goes in.\n- **Check for a different problem.** If this is about an ingestion or overdose, that needs toxicology or poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US), not a standing order.\n\nIf a standard dose is what you meant, I can enter it now."
      }
